{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Interactions.qbeta_counit_vs_trace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Interactions.qbeta_counit_vs_trace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QBetaCounitTrace.trMNP_bar_image","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QBetaCounitTrace.trMNP_bar_image","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/qbeta_counit_vs_trace.lean#L111-L117","doc":"**Markov-trace bar-decomposition.** `tr_M = h²/2 + (−h·z)` with `z`\nbar-even (`z ↦ z`). Under `h ↦ −h`: `tr_M(−h, z) = h²/2 + h·z` — even\nidentity part invariant, odd **loop/crossing** part `−h·z` flips sign. So\nthe odd channel of the observable is the Markov loop term; the bar-odd\ncarrier (KC15 `D(q)`) feeds it through this term, not the identity term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QBetaCounitTrace.epsNP_bar_image","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QBetaCounitTrace.epsNP_bar_image","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/qbeta_counit_vs_trace.lean#L104-L109","doc":"**Counit bar-image.** Under the bar flip `h ↦ −h`, `ε(−h) = h²/2 + h`:\nthe even part `h²/2` is invariant and the odd part `−h` flips to `+h`.\nRead against `epsNP_decomp` (`ε(h) = h²/2 − h`), this exhibits the split\n`ε = (bar-even h²/2) + (bar-odd −h)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QBetaCounitTrace.trMNP_decomp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QBetaCounitTrace.trMNP_decomp","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/qbeta_counit_vs_trace.lean#L99-L102","doc":"**Markov-trace bar-decomposition.** `tr_M = h²/2 + (−h·z)` — even identity\nterm plus odd loop term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QBetaCounitTrace.epsNP_decomp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QBetaCounitTrace.epsNP_decomp","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/qbeta_counit_vs_trace.lean#L92-L97","doc":"**Counit bar-decomposition.** `ε = h²/2 + (−h)`: an even part `h²/2` plus\nan odd part `−h`. Under `h ↦ −h` the even part is invariant and the odd\npart flips sign, so the odd channel of `Q_β` (built on `ε`) is exactly the\nunweighted crossing term `−h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QBetaCounitTrace.trMNP_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QBetaCounitTrace.trMNP_q","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/qbeta_counit_vs_trace.lean#L71-L76","doc":"**Markov-trace closed form in `q`** (via `h = q − q⁻¹`):\n`tr_M(n−p) = (q² − 1)(q² − 2qz − 1) / (2 q²)` — note **no** spurious\noverall factor of `z` (the identity `γ` carries weight `1`, not `z`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QBetaCounitTrace.epsNP_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QBetaCounitTrace.epsNP_q","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/qbeta_counit_vs_trace.lean#L63-L69","doc":"**Counit closed form in `q`** (via `h = q − q⁻¹`):\n`ε(n−p) = (q² − 1)(q² − 2q − 1) / (2 q²)`.\nThe `(2 : R) ≠ 0` hypothesis excludes characteristic `2`, where the\n`/2` in the mass normalisation is ill-defined. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QBetaCounitTrace.agree_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QBetaCounitTrace.agree_iff","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/qbeta_counit_vs_trace.lean#L52-L61","doc":"For `h ≠ 0`, the two functionals agree on the nucleon difference\n**iff** the Markov loop is trivial, `z = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QBetaCounitTrace.eps_sub_trMNP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QBetaCounitTrace.eps_sub_trMNP","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/qbeta_counit_vs_trace.lean#L48-L50","doc":"**The exact gap.** Counit minus Markov trace is `h·(z − 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QBetaCounitTrace.trMNP_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QBetaCounitTrace.trMNP_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/qbeta_counit_vs_trace.lean#L43-L46","doc":"**Coincidence at the trivial loop.** The counit is the Markov trace\nat `z = 1` (the `q`-stripped / topological limit). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QBetaCounitTrace.trMNP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QBetaCounitTrace.trMNP","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/qbeta_counit_vs_trace.lean#L38-L41","doc":"Markov trace of the `N=0` neutron−proton NF difference: identity\nweight `1` (axiom M1), each surviving crossing weighted by the loop\nvalue `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QBetaCounitTrace.epsNP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QBetaCounitTrace.epsNP","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/qbeta_counit_vs_trace.lean#L34-L36","doc":"Frobenius counit (augmentation) of the `N=0` neutron−proton NF\ndifference: every basis element weighted by `1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}